                    "In addition to the 10-day reporting requirement, STEM OPT students must complete a semi-annual self-validation in the SEVP Portal or through their DSO. This validation confirms that the student is still working for the reported employer, that the employment is directly related to their STEM degree, and that the terms and conditions of the Form I-983 Training Plan are being met.",
                    "Failure to complete reporting obligations or the semi-annual validation can result in the DSO recommending SEVIS termination. Once a SEVIS record is terminated, the student is considered out of status and must either apply for reinstatement or depart the United States. Given the serious consequences, STEM OPT students should set calendar reminders for their validation deadlines."
